  "notes": "The sun circle is a lighter tint of each band it crosses; drawn here in two tints. Not drawn: 'Lufthansa Group' small aft, registration and flags. A few aircraft may still wear the 2021 Eurowings Discover titles. On the A330 the blue block's diagonal sits further aft, following the fin. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on D-AIUW (A320, 2025): title place and length (0.236, behind the forward door) agree; lowercase 0.66 of the ascenders. The blue block's edge is a straight diagonal; the sun circle's arcs are densely sampled (24 points) between real corners at the bands, so left as polygons. The tail block's forward edge is a straight diagonal as seen from the side: its points along the line replaced by the two ends (2026-11-15).",
  "history": "New in the dataset (Skyarium v1 had no Discover entry). Replaced the Eurowings Discover scheme of 2021."
